# CI Feedback and Manual Preview Deploy

## Dual-mode testing (mandatory)

1. **GitHub Actions is not the only test source.** Canonical logic: `scripts/pipeline/run-local-quality-gates.sh`.
2. **Always run VM local quality gates** before asking the user to authorize preview deploy.
   - Gates are **never skippable**: a project `beforeShellExecution` hook (`.cursor/hooks/require-gates-before-deploy.sh`) blocks any preview-mutating command (`kubectl set image|apply|patch|scale|replace|create|delete|rollout restart`, `helm upgrade|install`, `BYPASS_CI=1`, the preview-deploy scripts) unless `scripts/pipeline/require-fresh-gates.sh` confirms `reports/pipeline/latest-summary.json` PASSED at the current `HEAD`. Both deploy scripts enforce the same check. Re-run gates after every commit before deploying.
3. If GitHub Actions shows billing/runner lock (0-step jobs), run VM gates and report **CI infrastructure failure** — not code pass/fail.
4. Present **both** GitHub CI (`collect-ci-feedback.sh`) and VM local results (`cursor-local-feedback.sh`).
5. Deploy only after explicit user approval.
6. If deploying on VM gates because GitHub CI unavailable, user must type **`AUTHORIZE DEPLOY WITH VM GATES`**.
7. Never introduce production mocks/stubs without allowlist (`test:no-stubs`).
8. No backend capability is complete without real frontend surfacing or documented internal-only status.
9. **Full vNext ≠ slice preview.** Do not call `impilo-preview` full vNext until `check-full-boot-runtime-completeness.sh` reports `FULL_BOOT_PASS`.
10. Full-boot deploy uses namespace `impilo-full-preview` and phrase `AUTHORIZE FULL BOOT PREVIEW DEPLOY` — never auto-deploy; never destroy the `impilo-preview` fallback namespace.
10b. **Highest-Validated-Stack-Wins.** The public IP `https://impilo.mohcc.gov.zw` serves the **latest validated preview generation**, not a fixed starter slice. The full stack (`impilo-full-preview`) owns the public ingress; the 4-service `impilo-preview` slice is a rollback fallback with `ingress.enabled: false`. Exactly **one** ingress claims the public entrypoint — verify with `scripts/operator/report-preview-generation.sh` (`SINGLE_PUBLIC_STACK: yes`). Each higher-count validated stack replaces the previous lower-count one as the public target; do not run permanent duplicate preview stacks.
11. All seven planes and all classified services must be discovered from registry (`docs/registry/services-registry.yaml`) — examples in prompts are not exhaustive.
12. **Runtime image strategy** gates full boot (`docs/environment/RUNTIME_IMAGE_STRATEGY_DOCTRINE.md`). Missing Dockerfile ≠ automatic failure; missing **required** strategy or failed required image build = blocking.
13. **Human sudo checkpoint:** When sudo is required, complete all possible non-sudo work first, then create a single checkpoint (`reports/full-boot/sudo-checkpoint.*`) with one product-owner terminal block (`sudo-checkpoint-run`). Product owner enters password only; then `sudo checkpoint completed` → `bash scripts/operator/fullboot.sh continue`. Do not push tmux/kubectl/helm/image-import orchestration onto the product owner. Sudo ≠ deploy authorization (`AUTHORIZE FULL BOOT PREVIEW DEPLOY`).

## Workflow

1. VM Remote SSH: `/opt/impilo/repos/Impilo-vNext`.
2. `bash scripts/pipeline/run-local-quality-gates.sh` before/after substantive changes.
3. Commit/push; `bash scripts/ci/collect-ci-feedback.sh` after push.
4. `bash scripts/pipeline/cursor-local-feedback.sh` for user decision.
5. **Do not auto-deploy preview** after push.
6. `bash scripts/deploy/manual-authorized-preview-deploy.sh` only after approval.
7. Post-deploy smoke + `/health/version` commit match.

